---
// The page a LinkedIn DM link unfurls into.
//
// WHY A PAGE AND NOT THE IMAGE URL. A bare .png does unfurl on LinkedIn, but with no OpenGraph
// tags to read it titles the card "web link", which is what a spam link looks like. The title
// and description have to come from a real HTML document, so this page exists mainly to carry
// three meta tags. It is also a reasonable thing to land on if somebody clicks through.
//
// THE CARD IMAGE is padded to 1200x627 (LinkedIn's 1.91:1) with a gradient matched to the
// artwork's own corners. At the source 792x612 LinkedIn crops or shrinks it, and the text in
// the comparison is too small to read either way.
//
// Scrapers do not run JavaScript, so everything the unfurl needs is in the server-rendered
// head. No tracking here on purpose: this is a preview target, and a page view from LinkedIn's
// crawler is not a person.
const OG_IMAGE = 'https://24214994.fs1.hubspotusercontent-na1.net/hubfs/24214994/volcano-assets/harvest-vs-workflowmax-og.png';
const FULL_IMAGE = 'https://24214994.fs1.hubspotusercontent-na1.net/hubfs/24214994/volcano-assets/harvest-vs-workflowmax-full.png';
// Same artwork re-rendered from the vector PDF at twice the size. A 792px image shown at 792
// CSS px is upscaled 2x on any high-DPI screen, which is most laptops, and that was the real
// cause of the blur. srcset lets a 1x screen keep the 696KB smaller file.
const FULL_IMAGE_2X = 'https://24214994.fs1.hubspotusercontent-na1.net/hubfs/24214994/volcano-assets/harvest-vs-workflowmax-full@2x.png';
const FULL_IMAGE_3X = 'https://24214994.fs1.hubspotusercontent-na1.net/hubfs/24214994/volcano-assets/harvest-vs-workflowmax-full@3x.png';
const TITLE = 'Harvest vs. WorkflowMAX';
const DESC = 'Same job, two very different ways to get it done. From enquiry to invoice, one connected platform or a collection of tools.';
const URL = 'https://lp.workflowmax.com/app/harvest';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
  <title>{TITLE}</title>
  <meta name="description" content={DESC} />

  <!-- OpenGraph: what LinkedIn, Slack and the rest read to build the preview card. -->
  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <meta property="og:url" content={URL} />
  <meta property="og:title" content={TITLE} />
  <meta property="og:description" content={DESC} />
  <meta property="og:image" content={OG_IMAGE} />
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="627" />
  <meta property="og:image:alt" content="Side by side: a disconnected set of tools against one connected platform, from lead to invoice." />
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="WorkflowMAX" />

  <!-- Twitter/X reads its own namespace; summary_large_image gives the full-width card. -->
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
  <meta name="twitter:title" content={TITLE} />
  <meta name="twitter:description" content={DESC} />
  <meta name="twitter:image" content={OG_IMAGE} />

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:opsz,wght@9..40,400;9..40,500;9..40,700&display=swap" />
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: dark; }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: #04140e;
      color: #EAF4F0;
      font-family: 'DM Sans', -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.55;
    }
    .wrap { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding-block: 40px; padding-left: 20px; padding-right: 20px; }
    h1 { font-size: clamp(26px, 4vw, 40px); line-height: 1.12; margin: 0 0 10px; letter-spacing: -0.015em; text-wrap: balance; }
    .sub { color: #9DB9AE; font-size: clamp(15px, 2vw, 17px); margin: 0 0 28px; max-width: 62ch; }
    figure { margin: 0 0 28px; }
    /* Widened on request so the comparison reads at a glance. The 792px source cannot carry
       this on its own, so srcset offers the same artwork re-rendered from the vector PDF at
       1584 and 2376px and the browser takes what its pixel density needs. */
    img { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 1060px; height: auto; margin: 0 auto;
          border-radius: 14px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1); }
    .cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; }
    a.btn {
      display: inline-block; padding: 13px 26px; border-radius: 100px; font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 15px; text-decoration: none; transition: background .2s, border-color .2s;
    }
    a.primary { background: #63DB94; color: #0A2F28; }
    a.primary:hover { background: #45c97e; }
    a.ghost { border: 1px solid rgba(99,219,148,.4); color: #63DB94; }
    a.ghost:hover { background: rgba(99,219,148,.08); border-color: #63DB94; }
    a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #63DB94; outline-offset: 3px; }
    footer { margin-top: 40px; padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1); color: #6E8B80; font-size: 12.5px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="wrap">
    <h1>Same job. Two very different ways to get it done.</h1>
    <p class="sub">From enquiry to invoice, one connected platform or a collection of tools. Every handoff
      between tools burns time and hides what a job actually made.</p>

    <figure>
      <img src={FULL_IMAGE_2X}
                srcset={`${FULL_IMAGE} 792w, ${FULL_IMAGE_2X} 1584w, ${FULL_IMAGE_3X} 2376w`}
                sizes="(max-width: 1100px) calc(100vw - 40px), 1060px"
                width="792" height="612"
                alt="Left: a disconnected set of tools, with the lead in a CRM, the quote in a spreadsheet, time in Harvest and invoicing in Xero, joined by manual handoffs. Right: WorkflowMAX running the full job lifecycle in one place, from lead and quote through to job, timesheets, invoicing and AI-integrated reporting." />
    </figure>

    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn primary" href="https://app.workflowmax.com/register/sign_up">Start a free trial</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://workflowmax.com">Explore WorkflowMAX</a>
    </div>

    <footer>WorkflowMAX runs the whole job lifecycle in one place, from the lead through to the final invoice.</footer>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
